      "message": "Nice - thanks for adding this. This helped me figure out what this was such a problem for you with the flask work (before is wasn\u0027t quite apparent to me).\n\nFor API contracts, is a HTTP 404 Not Found with application/json the same as HTTP 404 Not Found with text/html?\n\nI assume if HTTP 404 Not Found with text/html is built into a framework and probably the correct way to do things and out homegrown implementation was probably wrong. But does that technically classify as a backwards incompatible change? Or is it really just the http status code?",
